@startuml
title Deploiement Application - Sequence Complete

actor Admin
participant "gandal_deploy.py" as script
participant "API Kubernetes" as api
database etcd
participant Scheduler
participant Kubelet
participant Containerd
participant Registry

== Phase 1: Namespace ==
Admin -> script : python gandal_deploy.py deploy\nalice memoire my-api ...
script -> api : Create Namespace\nproject-alice-memoire
api -> etcd : Store namespace

== Phase 2-4: Gouvernance ==
script -> api : Create LimitRange\n(default: 500m CPU, 512Mi RAM)
script -> api : Create ResourceQuota\n(4 pods, 2 CPU, 2Gi RAM)
script -> api : Create NetworkPolicy\n(isolation)

== Phase 5: Deployment ==
script -> api : Create Deployment\n(replicas: 2, image: localhost:5000/my-api:v1)
api -> Scheduler : Schedule 2 pods
Scheduler -> Kubelet : Assign pod1 to node
Scheduler -> Kubelet : Assign pod2 to node

== Phase 6: Pull Image ==
Kubelet -> Containerd : Pull image
Containerd -> Registry : GET localhost:5000/my-api:v1
Registry --> Containerd : Image layers
Containerd -> Containerd : Extract and prepare

== Phase 7: Start Pods ==
Kubelet -> Containerd : Create containers
Containerd --> Kubelet : Containers started
Kubelet -> Kubelet : Execute readinessProbe\n(tcpSocket:80)
Kubelet -> api : Update pod status: Running + Ready

== Phase 8-9: Service + Ingress ==
script -> api : Create Service\n(ClusterIP, port 80)
script -> api : Create Ingress\n(host: my-api-memoire-alice.16.170.20.250.sslip.io)

== Phase 10: Verification ==
script -> api : Wait for Ready condition
api --> script : 2/2 pods Ready

script --> Admin : Success!\nURL: http://my-api-memoire-alice.16.170.20.250.sslip.io

@enduml
